   "id": "root",
   "x": 293,
   "y": 10,
   "w": 760,
   "kind": "dark",
   "title": "Peptic ulcer disease: WHICH ulcer, and HOW MUCH acid suppression?",
   "lines": [
    "an ulcer goes through the whole mucosa (muscularis mucosae too); less is an erosion · acid + pepsin overwhelm the defences",
    "GASTRITIS behind it: ACUTE from non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs), steroids, alcohol, severe stress (burns, shock, sepsis) · CHRONIC from H. pylori (commonest), autoimmune, chemical"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_ulc",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 156,
   "w": 484,
   "h": 60,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "THE ULCER: stomach or duodenum?",
   "lines": [
    "the TIMING of the pain points the way"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_drug",
   "x": 569,
   "y": 156,
   "w": 732,
   "h": 60,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "THE DRUG: how much acid suppression?",
   "lines": [
    "strongest to weakest: PPI → H2 blocker → antacid"
   ]
  },
